#: admin/class-admin.php:174
msgid "When administrators use the AI translation features in Loco Translate, source strings and translation parameters are sent directly to the AI service provider chosen by the administrator (OpenRouter, an administrator-configured OpenAI endpoint, a self-hosted or remote Ollama instance, or a custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint). When using OpenRouter, your site URL and site title are also transmitted in standard HTTP request headers for usage attribution. No visitor personal data or frontend tracking information is collected or transmitted."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-page.php:28
msgid "AI Service Transparency & Data Transmission Disclosure"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-page.php:31
msgid "This plugin connects to external AI services (OpenRouter, OpenAI, a self-hosted/remote Ollama instance, or an administrator-configured OpenAI-compatible endpoint) ONLY when an administrator explicitly initiates a translation or connection test. Source strings, context, and translation instructions are sent directly from your WordPress server to the configured endpoint. No Error Web Agency-operated intermediary or proxy server is used. Services such as OpenRouter may route requests to downstream model providers according to their own terms and data policies."
msgstr ""

